# Copy this file to .env and fill in a key to upgrade the AI Chat Assistant
# from extractive answers (free, offline, built from /data reference docs)
# to fully generative, conversational answers.
#
# Nothing here is required — the backend runs fine with none of these set.
# Recommended free option if you don't have a paid API key: OpenRouter or
# Groq (both have generous free tiers) or Ollama (fully local, no signup).

# Which provider to use. Leave unset to auto-detect from whichever API key
# below is present. Set to "none" to force extractive-only mode even if a
# key is set.
# AI_PROVIDER=openai

# --- OpenAI (paid) --------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# --- Anthropic (paid) ------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-3-5-haiku-20241022

# --- OpenRouter (free tier available) --------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys — the default model below
# ("openrouter/free") auto-picks a free model for you; override with any
# specific model from https://openrouter.ai/models if you prefer.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openrouter/free

# --- Groq (free tier available, very fast) ---------------------------------
# Get a key at https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# --- Ollama (fully local, genuinely free, no signup) -----------------------
# Install from https://ollama.com, run `ollama pull llama3.1`, then
# `ollama serve` (usually already running as a background service).
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1

# --- Any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint -----------------------------------
# AI_BASE_URL=https://your-provider.example.com/v1
# AI_API_KEY=...
# AI_MODEL=...

# --- Web search (optional, free tier available) -----------------------------
# When set, the assistant can search the live web to fill gaps the curated
# Data Docs don't cover, and cites real, clickable links back to the user.
# Only fires when local retrieval looks weak or the question is clearly
# web-shaped (e.g. "look up...", "current price of..."), so normal
# Data-Doc-grounded questions never spend a search.
# Get a free key at https://app.tavily.com (1,000 searches/month, no card).
# TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-...

# --- Server ---------------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=4000
